  "narrative": {
    "text": "Figure A.1, 'Semantic governance capabilities, the roles that carry them out, and the supporting application components' (Appendix F, Semantic Governance Infrastructure: capability details). Five capabilities run left to right as a flow: Consume, Change requests, Change management, Publication and Monitoring. The step from Change management to Publication is drawn dashed. Roles and information objects are attached above: Stakeholder to Consume; Author and Owner to Change management; Content and Upstream content to Publication; and Management rules to Monitoring. Supporting tools are attached below: Change-request tooling to Change requests, Authoring to Change management, and Repository to Publication. A legend distinguishes the three types: capability, role or information object, and supporting tool.",
